ment flow, confirmation screen — ideally via Playwright screenshots once a working Chromium binary is available.\n   - Run `pnpm nx lint cinescope` and fix any lint errors (not yet done).\n   - Run `pnpm nx test cinescope` and ensure the existing `app.spec.tsx` (and any other tests) still pass (not yet done) — note `app.spec.tsx` renders `<App />` inside `<BrowserRouter>`, but `App` itself no longer needs an outer `BrowserRouter` wrapper conflict since `main.tsx` already provides one separately; should double check this still renders fine since `BookingProvider`/`ToastProvider` are now inside `App`.\n   - Double-check all 69 acceptance criteria (AC-01 through AC-69) systematically against the implementation, particularly:\n     - AC-08 (global column numbering identical across rows) — needs visual confirmation\n     - AC-14 (couch visually distinct, \"at least twice as wide as a seat\") — implemented via `columnSpan` over 2 tracks, needs visual confirmation\n     - AC-56/AC-57 (subtitle format and centering of seat-limit-info text)\n     - AC-65 (required field labels end with ` *`, phone label does not) — implemented as literal strings \"First name *\" etc.\n     - All `data-testid` attributes in section 9 — need a careful line-by-line audit against section 9.1–9.7 of spec/README.md, since these are exact-contract requirements (e.g., I should double check `summary-item-row` doesn't need \"Row\" prefix text — I already fixed this earlier to contain ONLY the row number, matching the apparent intent of section 9.7's \"contains only\" pattern even though summary-item-row wasn't explicitly listed in that rule).\n   - Mark the checkboxes in `/workspace/project/spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md` through `07-final-pass.md` as complete (ticked) once each ticket's acceptance criteria are verified — the ticket spec states \"A ticket is done when every box in it is ticked and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds,\" implying I should edit these markdown checkbox files, though this wasn't explicitly re-confirmed as in-scope since the main task framing says \"Finish only when every ticket is done\" which could be interpreted as the ACs being satisfied rather than literally editing checkbox files — I should use judgment here, likely ticking the boxes is the clean way to show/track completion and matches the ticket system's own definition of \"done.\"\n   - Final pass (ticket 07): walk through the whole flow against the spec and fix mismatches, then confirm `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds one final time.\n   - Clean up scratch testing artifacts (`/tmp/pw-test`, any `/tmp/pw-browsers`, `/tmp/dev.log`, `/tmp/api.log`) — these are outside the repo and don't need git cleanup, but background dev/api server processes should probably be stopped before declaring the task complete (or left running if useful for final manual verification — no explicit instruction either way).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary was requested, I was deep in troubleshooting how to get a headless Chromium browser working via Playwright in this sandboxed environment, in order to visually verify the app (per the system instruction: \"For UI or frontend changes, start the dev server and use the feature in a browser before reporting the task as complete\"). \n\n   Sequence of the most recent actions:\n   1. Confirmed pre-installed Chromium at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234` exists but doesn't match playwright npm package version requirements (tried 1.48.2 needing rev 1140, then latest 1.64.1 needing rev 1248).\n   2. `npx playwright install chromium` with default `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/opt/ms-playwright` failed: `EACCES: permission denied, mkdir '/opt/ms-playwright/__dirlock'`.\n   3. Retried with `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/tmp/pw-browsers` (after `mkdir -p /tmp/pw-browsers`) — download reached 100% of 190.5 MiB twice but failed both times with `ENOSPC: no space left on device, write`.\n   4. Ran `df -h /tmp /opt / 2>/dev/null` revealing `/tmp` is `tmp